    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114695,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:41:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114696,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:41:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114697,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases affect the posterior mandible. Maxillary SOCs tend to lie anteriorly.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:41:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114698,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SOC presents as swelling that occasionally grows rapidly. Most cases are asymptomatic, with only a few mandibular examples characterized by paraesthesia.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Radiographically, SOC is a poorly defined radiolucency with cortical bone destruction and occasional tooth mobility. Tumour extension beyond radiographic margins has been reported in many cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:41:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114699,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a very slight female predilection. The age at diagnosis ranges from 31&nbsp;to 73&nbsp;years, with the majority of cases arising in the fifth to seventh decades of life {33715971}. SOC may be underrecognized or may have been described under another name {21418400}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:41:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114700,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:41:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114701,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:41:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114702,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dense fibrous tissue fragments</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:41:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114703,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A dense, fibrocollagenous sclerotic stroma is the hallmark of SOC, containing malignant epithelial cells forming single-file thin cords, strands, small nests, and infrequent islands of more epidermoid cells {18753945}. Only mild cellular atypia has been observed in most cases. SOCs are infiltrative and lack encapsulation. Perineural or intraneural invasion is frequently seen, but lymphovascular invasion is rare. Mitotic activity is inconspicuous and necrosis is rare. Mucus-negative clear cells may be present, but glandular differentiation has also been reported {33715971}. Calcifications including cementum-like bone, bone, or dentinoid have been observed in half of the cases.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>There is no specific immunohistochemical marker for SOC. The epithelial component is highlighted by CK5/6, CK14, CK19, and p63.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:41:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114704,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:41:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114705,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>All cases studied have been negative for <em>EWSR1</em> rearrangement.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:41:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114706,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> malignant odontogenic carcinoma with infiltrating thin cords and nests of epithelium; sclerotic stroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> mild atypia; perineural/intraneural infiltration (often prominent).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:23:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114707,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "<p >There is no defined eighth-edition Union for International Cancer Control (UICC)&nbsp;/ American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM staging system staging guidance, but the use of International Collaboration on Cancer Reporting (ICCR) minimum data set reporting is encouraged {30500289}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:23:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114708,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 145,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "<p>To date, the prognosis has been excellent, with only local recurrence in a few cases despite perineural invasion. Exceedingly rare recurrence and metastasis have been reported {37080825}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-10T12:39:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]